        "TileImage": "$($repository c04167bc-f321-4e0b-be51-0b5e662d2669).Image",
        "Description": "Taheji Koyama, known as &quot;The Controller&quot; is the final member of the 1990s SIGMA team. His role on the team was as logistics and operations coordination, and his meticulous attention to every detail enabled SIGMA operations to go off without a hitch in even the most chaotic of situations. Known as a man who always had a backup plan for when his primary plan failed, Koyama retired from CICADA in 1998. He moved to a small estate in the mountains of the Nagano Prefecture. In recent years, he has dedicated himself to various philanthropic pursuits, including support for war-crimes victims across Asia. A year ago, he was diagnosed with Elyen’s Syndrome, an extremely rare genetic disorder, but chose not to seek medical treatment, although he could well afford it, choosing rather to continue to support various charities. Approximately two weeks after the receipt of the SIGMA contracts, he abruptly pulled all support from all of the charities, he had formerly supported, and had himself moved to",
